{:edb/db-before-t 914 :edb/db-after-t 915 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534227 50 #inst "2026-10-11T17:58:34.473Z" 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186179735 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414917 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186179735 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414918 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186179735 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414926 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186179736 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414923 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186179736 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414924 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186179736 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414925 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186179736 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414927 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186179737 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414919 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186179737 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414920 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186179737 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414921 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186179737 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414922 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186179737 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414928 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186179864 1050 1080.0 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186180012 1068 #edb/ref 17592186177741 13194139534227 17592186045417 false] [17592186180012 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414904 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186180012 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186180012 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_(C)F \\cdot dr$, where $F(x, y) = \\cos xi + \\sin yj$ and $C$ is the curve $y = 2x^{2} - 1$ traversed from the point $A(1, 1)$ to the point $B(2, 7)$?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t) = ti + (2t^{2} - 1)j$.*" 13194139534227 17592186045417 false] [17592186180012 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j$ and $C$ is the curve $y=2{x}^{2}-1$ traversed from the point $A(1,1)$ to the point $B(2,7)?$\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=t\\,i+(2{t}^{2}-1)\\,j.$*" 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186180012 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize the curve. This is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =t\\,i+(2{t}^{2}-1)\\,j,\\,1\\le t\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t,\\,y=2{t}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{t}^{2}-1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}-1)j \\\\  & =i+4t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{t}^{2}-1)\\,j)\\cdot (i+4t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{t}^{2}-1)\\cdot 4t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{t}^{2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2{t}^{2}-1)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186180015 1068 #edb/ref 17592186177759 13194139534227 17592186045417 false] [17592186180015 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414910 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186180015 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186180015 1071 "Evaluate ${∮}_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=y\\,i-x\\,j$ and $C$ is a circle of radius $1$ centered at the origin, traversed once in the counterclockwise direction." 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186180015 1071 "Evaluate $∮_(C)F(r) \\cdot dr$, where $F(x, y) = yi - xj$ and $C$ is a circle of radius $1$ centered at the origin, traversed once in the counterclockwise direction." 13194139534227 17592186045417 false] [17592186180015 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize a circle of radius $1$ centered at the origin. It can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =y\\,i-x\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =-{sin}^{2}⁡t-{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =-({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-1)\\,dt \\\\  & ={-t|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186180172 1068 #edb/ref 17592186178576 13194139534227 17592186045417 false] [17592186180172 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414912 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186180172 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186180172 1071 "![](images/48/4807f92defb4202359a32ca046073cd138db396a0975164e42b96126ac0cc591.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to $\\displaystyle \\int_(C)F \\cdot dr$, where $F(x, y) = e^{x}i + e^{-2y}j$ and $C$ is the arc of a circle of radius $1$ centered at the origin traversed counterclockwise from the point $(1, 0)$ to the point $(0, 1)$?\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t) = \\cos ti + \\sin tj$.*" 13194139534227 17592186045417 false] [17592186180172 1071 "![](images/48/4807f92defb4202359a32ca046073cd138db396a0975164e42b96126ac0cc591.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\,i+{e}^{-2y}\\,j$ and $C$ is the arc of a circle of radius $1$ centered at the origin traversed counterclockwise from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(0,1)?$\n\n*Hint: Use the parametrization $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j.$*" 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186180172 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to parameterize a part-circle of radius $1$ centered at the origin. This curve can be parameterized as \n\n$$\nr(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, along the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & ={e}^{x}\\,i+{e}^{-2y}\\,j \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,i+{e}^{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,i+{e}^{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+{e}^{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186414827 1080 "72{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt" 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186414827 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186414827 1083 #uuid "00790b3e-1877-50c1-bfcc-d335a0c8a0b2" 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186414828 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t(t+4{e}^{2t})\\,dt" 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186414828 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186414828 1083 #uuid "02315312-3684-5faa-a71f-6939225f794e" 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186414829 1080 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186414829 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186414829 1083 #uuid "02e28cc7-f7f3-51e1-bea0-158eef714f3a" 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186414830 1080 "{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}+et)\\,dt" 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186414830 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186414830 1083 #uuid "04de95bf-b731-52c7-8b53-b252f4ea7fbe" 13194139534227 17592186045417 true] [17592186414831 1080 "-\\frac{7}{4}" 13194139534227 17592186045417 